<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired"><h2>What it inspired</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Hail, Gladdening Light (John Keble)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1834</span><span class="sg-chain-h">translation</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Sebaste (John Stainer)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1875</span><span class="sg-chain-h">tune written for Keble's translation, in Hymns Ancient and Modern</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Hail, Gladdening Light (Charles Wood)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1912</span><span class="sg-chain-h">anthem for eight voices on Keble's translation</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Translation (Henry Wadsworth Longfellow)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">translation</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Translation (Robert Bridges)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">translation, sung to music by Louis Bourgeois</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Book of Common Prayer (Episcopal Church)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1979</span><span class="sg-chain-h">prose translation as an optional invitatory canticle</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">St Gabriel (F. A. G. Ouseley)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">hymn tune</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Christ Church (E. S. Medley)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">hymn tune</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">All-Night Vigil, Op. 52 (Pyotr Ilyich Tchaikovsky)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">setting in Church Slavonic</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Evening Hymn (Arthur Sullivan)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">setting</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Op. 23, No. 3 (Alexander Gretchaninov)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">setting in Church Slavonic</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">All-Night Vigil, Op. 37 (Sergei Rachmaninoff)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">setting in Church Slavonic</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Anthem (Geoffrey Shaw)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">setting</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Op. 28 (Craig Sellar Lang)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">setting</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Phos Hilaron (Alexander Flood)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">setting</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Church Music (David Crowder Band)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2009</span><span class="sg-chain-h">setting</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">O Gracious Light (Mason Shefa)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2012</span><span class="sg-chain-h">setting</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Phos Hilaron (Byzantine Theme), Civilization V: Gods &amp; Kings (Geoff Knorr)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2012</span><span class="sg-chain-h">setting for a video game</span></li></ul></section>
